# TM7: {{^}}msil-ld: error: managed call '[[F]]': parameter [[I]] passes [[N]] bits for '[[E]]', which is not an enum of that width{{$}}

## T-M7 for each parameter on its own: a handle beside an integer. msil-ld's
## lines are sorted, so that the pins hold whatever order the stubs are
## checked in, and any other line fails.
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj -mtriple=x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-msil pairs.ll -o pairs.o
# RUN: not msil-ld pairs.o --reference=refs -o x.exe 2>&1 | sort | %{err} --check-prefix=PAIRS
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj -mtriple=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-msil pairs.ll -o pairs-lnx.o
# RUN: not msil-ld pairs-lnx.o --reference=refs -o x.exe 2>&1 | sort | %{err} --check-prefix=PAIRS
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj -mtriple=msil64-unknown-dotnet pairs.ll -o pairs-net.o
# RUN: not msil-ld pairs-net.o --reference=refs -o x.exe 2>&1 | sort | %{err} --check-prefix=PAIRS
# RUN: not ls x.exe
# PAIRS:      {{^}}msil-ld: error: managed call 'mode_pair': parameter 2 passes 64 bits for 'Contoso.Mode', which is not an enum of that width{{$}}
# PAIRS-NEXT: {{^}}msil-ld: error: managed call 'mode_rev': parameter 1 passes 64 bits for 'Contoso.Mode', which is not an enum of that width{{$}}
# PAIRS-NEXT: {{^}}msil-ld: error: managed call 'pair_cmp': parameter 2 passes 64 bits for 'Contoso.Point', which is not an enum of that width{{$}}
# PAIRS-NEXT: {{^}}msil-ld: error: managed call 'pair_rev': parameter 1 passes 64 bits for 'Contoso.Point', which is not an enum of that width{{$}}
